From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 102/102] cheetah: ship a KernelSU Next init_boot when one is
 given

With CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT set, init_boot is that prebuilt (the build's own
init_boot patched by KernelSU Next's ksud) instead of one made from the
generic ramdisk. The build system re-signs it with the init_boot AVB key and
puts it in target-files, so the fastboot images and the OTA both carry it and
root survives updates. Unset, nothing changes. Only ExpressiveOS's build
sets it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cheetah/BoardConfig.mk | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk b/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
index 9b505ca..e7661be 100644
--- a/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -32,3 +32,12 @@ BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX :=
 
 # KernelSU Next manager (ExpressiveOS only): libksud.so is a program
 TARGET_FS_CONFIG_GEN += device/google/pantah/ksu/config.fs
+
+# KernelSU Next (ExpressiveOS only): expressiveos-cheetah/ksu/tools/ksu-images.sh
+# builds once, patches that build's init_boot with KernelSU Next
+# (cheetah-ksu.sh), then builds again with CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT set, so the
+# images and the OTA ship the patched init_boot (re-signed with the tree's
+# init_boot AVB key like a built one).
+ifneq ($(CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT),)
+BOARD_PREBUILT_INIT_BOOT_IMAGE := $(CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT)
+endif
